  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1043 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nA couple chilly nights are on tap Thursday and Friday night, with\nfrost and/or freeze headlines likely to be needed in many \nlocations. Far northeast Oklahoma and northwest Arkansas are most \nlikely to see a freeze Thursday night, with a larger part of the \nforecast area likely to see a freeze Friday night. A hard freeze \nmay occur in some places Friday night, especially in far northeast\nOklahoma and northwest Arkansas.\n\nA storm system will move across the area late Saturday night and\nSunday bringing an increase in rain chances. There is some\nquestion how far north and east any rain spreads during the day \nSunday due to dry low level air continuing to advect into the \narea from the east, but many places will see at least light \namounts of rainfall Sunday. The best chance for 1/4 to 1/2 inch of\nrain will be across parts of southeast Oklahoma in the McAlester \nand Hugo areas. Temperatures will remain quite cool during the day\nSunday with the clouds and rain.\n\nQuiet weather returns early next week with a gradual warming\ntrend. Another storm system may increase rain chances again during\nthe latter half of next week.",
